      NoContraction in SPIR-V, `precise` in GLSL (no fused multiply-add, no reassociation)
  each value: its range, the derived error bound, the algorithm:
      f64(a)*f64(b)                            [1, 4]                   0 u^2          2Prod (exact)
      f64(a)*f64(b) - f64(c)                   [-3, 3]                  3 u^2          DWPlusFP
  derivation (u = 2^-24; RN rounds to nearest; a pair x~ = xh + xl has |xl| <= u |xh|):
    2Sum(a, b): s = RN(a + b), a' = RN(s - b), b' = RN(s - a'), t = RN((a - a') + (b - b')):
      s + t = a + b exactly (Knuth), |t| <= u |s|
    Fast2Sum(a, b): s = RN(a + b), t = RN(b - RN(s - a)): s + t = a + b exactly when |a| >= |b| (Dekker)
    2Prod(a, b): p = RN(a b), e = fma(a, b, -p): p + e = a b exactly while |a b| >= 2^-102
      (a b - p is a multiple of ulp(a) ulp(b) below ulp(p): representable), |e| <= u |a b|
    DWPlusFP(x~, y): (sh, sl) = 2Sum(xh, y); v = RN(xl + sl); (zh, zl) = Fast2Sum(sh, v):
      zh + zl = x~ + y + d (xl + sl), |d| <= u: the error is at most u (u |xh| + u |sh|),
      2.000 u^2 |x~ + y| when no cancellation (kappa = 1), (1 + kappa) u^2 in general;
      whatever cancels, by cases on xh and y: of opposite signs with |y| in [|xh|/2, 2|xh|],
      xh + y is a float (Sterbenz), so sl = 0, v = xl and the sum is exact; otherwise
      |xh + y| > |xh|/2 and the error is below 3 u^2 / (1 - 2u) = 3.000 u^2 |x~ + y| (the paper:
      2 u^2); Fast2Sum's precondition holds in both
    composition: a product's errors multiply (1 + ex)(1 + ey)(1 + e) - 1, a quotient's (1 + ex)(1 + e) / (1 - ey) - 1,
      a sum's are kappa max(ex, ey) + e (1 + kappa max(ex, ey)), a square root halves its operand's
  conditions:
    finite inputs (an infinity or a NaN gives NaN where f64 would carry it)
    no overflow: the largest value is 4, below 2^127 (derived from the ranges)
    no underflow: the 1 error-free product stays above 2^-102 (derived from the ranges)
    Fast2Sum's precondition |a| >= |b|: derived in each use from the magnitudes above
