> qa(x: f32) = f32(f16(x))
> foldproof qa
foldproof qa under gt1030: 1 conversion round trip the driver folds
  f32(f16(x)): gt1030 folds f32 -> f16 -> f32, so the card computes the operand itself
    the program relies on the rounding: at x=-3.40282347e+38: the program expects -inf, the folded one gives -3.40282347e+38
    fold-proof: asfloat((t1 >> 0x17 < 113 ? asuint(5.96046448e-08f32(t4 + ((1 << t3 - 1) - 1) + (t4 >> t3 & 1) >> t3)) : t1 > 2139095040 ? t1 : t2 >= 1199570944 ? 2139095040 : t2) | asuint(x) & 0x80000000) where t1 = asuint(x) & 0x7fffffff, t2 = t1 + 4095 + (t1 >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000, t3 = min(126 - (t1 >> 0x17), 25), t4 = t1 & 0x7fffff | 0x800000
      cost 40 under gt1030 (the round trip as written would be 6; folded it is 0 and does not round)
    proof:
      1. between 2^-14 and 2^16 the f16 values of a binade are the f32 values whose 13 low mantissa
         bits are 0; the bit pattern grows with |x| and a carry out of the mantissa is the next
         binade's first value, so rounding the value to f16 (nearest, ties to even) is rounding
         the pattern to a multiple of 2^13 (nearest, ties to the even quotient)
      2. (b + 4095 + (b >> 13 & 1)) & ~8191 is that rounding of b, for every 32-bit b: against
         q = b >> 13, r = b mod 2^13, (q + (r > 2^12 or r = 2^12 and q odd)) << 13: proved by SAT (both sides bit-blasted)
      3. a pattern rounded to 2^16 or more is infinity (|x| >= 65520 rounds past the largest f16);
         a NaN stays a NaN; the sign is put back
      4. below 2^-14 the f16 grid is fixed at 2^-24: with exponent field e the significand
         (1.m, 24 bits) loses k = 126 - e bits (at most 25: more leave 0); the quotient q is
         (sig + 2^(k-1) - 1 + (sig >> k & 1)) >> k, for every sig and k in 14..25 against its
         definition: proved by SAT (both sides bit-blasted); q <= 2^10, so f32(q) * 2^-24 is exact
    check (not the proof): 92672 bit patterns, both signs, exponent fields 0..255, ties and their
      neighbours at every mantissa bit: all equal to the evaluator's round trip
  defined qa_fp = asfloat((t1 >> 0x17 < 113 ? asuint(5.96046448e-08f32(t4 + ((1 << t3 - 1) - 1) + (t4 >> t3 & 1) >> t3)) : t1 > 2139095040 ? t1 : t2 >= 1199570944 ? 2139095040 : t2) | asuint(x) & 0x80000000) where t1 = asuint(x) & 0x7fffffff, t2 = t1 + 4095 + (t1 >> 13 & 1) & 0xffffe000, t3 = min(126 - (t1 >> 0x17), 25), t4 = t1 & 0x7fffff | 0x800000
